			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 671,
				"data": "\n\tThe predecessor never decides a space: a tag after a comment, a <br />, a control-flow\n\tblock or a predecessor that renders multiline takes its per-width wrap exactly as an inline\n\telement or component does there, so the authored space is kept and the pair packs — where\n\tprettier breaks its line between two tags with the container. The newline spelling of the\n\tsame boundary is held, so the two spellings are two fixed points. Only a block element\n\tpredecessor keeps the tag off its line; a comment or a control-flow block after the pair\n\ttakes the space as its own per-width wrap (inline_sibling_space_before_bounding); a\n\tdeclaration tag takes its own line.\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 671,
				"end": 673,
				"raw": "\n\n",
				"data": "\n\n"
			},
